  "metadata": {
    "source": "R. E. Treharne, A. Seymour-Pierce, K. Durose, K. Hutchings, S. Roncallo, D. Lane. Optical design and fabrication of fully sputtered CdTe/CdS solar cells. J. Phys: Conf. Ser. 286, 012038, (2011) (https://doi.org/10.1088/1742-6596/286/1/012038) (Numerical data kindly provided Dr. Robert Treharne); downloaded from refractiveindex.info",
    "description": "A CdS film was deposited on to a soda-lime glass substrate using RF magnetron sputtering. A variable-angle ellipsometer was used to take amplitude and phase change measurements. The refractive index and extinction coefficient was extracted from a multi-oscillator model fit to the ellipsometry data, as a function of wavelength, from 300 to 1500 nm"
  },
